# Oracle: VD cir-nodes (`ground` ties its names to node 0, top level only; ground nodes are
# global); INV-semantics 11.01 (`gnd` is no ground by default). A statement with no meaning
# left is an Inert opaque (R15).
# codes: S0003 S0003
file "ground_global.sim" deck
  title "ground and global nodes"
  opaque vacask inert "ground gnd agnd"
  global vdd vss
  opaque vacask inert "global (agnd)"
